From d64544e8e08fc4d8d5e117dfc61d831154ddc6b2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sebastian Huang <sebastian_huang@accton.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 16:51:31 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] mtk: mt76: schedule non-AQL TXQs on the hw of the station

When a station drops below MT_MAX_NON_AQL_PKT pending non-AQL frames,
mt76_tx_check_non_aql() schedules all its TXQs again, always on
dev->hw. On a DBDC device such as mt7915 (MT7981) the second band has
its own ieee80211_hw, so the TXQs of its stations were added to the
active TXQ list of the first band, under the first band's lock, while
the second band's scheduler used them on its own list:

  list_add corruption. next->prev should be prev (ffffff80036c1380), but was ffffff80036b1380. (next=ffffff80068900b8).
  WARNING: CPU: 1 PID: 1128 at __list_add_valid_or_report+0x74/0xd4
  Call trace:
   __list_add_valid_or_report
   __ieee80211_schedule_txq
   __mt76_tx_complete_skb
   mt76_connac2_txwi_free
   mt7915_mac_tx_free
   mt7915_rx_check
   mt76_dma_rx_poll

Use the hw of the station's band. On devices with one hw for all
radios (mt7996) this is the same hw as before.

The code came with upstream commit 2eb5d1e3 ("wifi: mt76: don't return
TXQ when exceeding max non-AQL packets") and is unchanged upstream.
---
 tx.c | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/tx.c b/tx.c
index 808ebe74..22f59e2a 100644
--- a/tx.c
+++ b/tx.c
@@ -236,6 +236,7 @@ mt76_tx_check_non_aql(struct mt76_dev *dev, struct mt76_wcid *wcid,
 {
 	struct ieee80211_tx_info *info = IEEE80211_SKB_CB(skb);
 	struct ieee80211_sta *sta;
+	struct ieee80211_hw *hw;
 	int pending;
 	int i;
 
@@ -250,11 +251,15 @@ mt76_tx_check_non_aql(struct mt76_dev *dev, struct mt76_wcid *wcid,
 	if (!sta || pending != MT_MAX_NON_AQL_PKT - 1)
 		return;
 
+	/* the TXQs belong to the hw of the station's band, which is not
+	 * dev->hw for the second band of a DBDC device such as mt7915
+	 */
+	hw = mt76_dev_phy(dev, wcid->phy_idx)->hw;
 	for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(sta->txq); i++) {
 		if (!sta->txq[i])
 			continue;
 
-		ieee80211_schedule_txq(dev->hw, sta->txq[i]);
+		ieee80211_schedule_txq(hw, sta->txq[i]);
 	}
 }
 
